## Creating Tasking Documents

When creating task assignments, you MUST include:

### Role Assignment Section (MANDATORY)
Every tasking document must start with a Role Assignment section:
- List all roles needed for the sprint/tasks
- Use table format: Role | Status | Assigned Agent | Tasks | Dependencies
- Status values: Available / In Progress / Complete / Blocked
- Enable new agents to identify and claim available work

### Dependency Tracking (MANDATORY)
Each task must include:
- Dependencies section listing prerequisite tasks with status
- Requirement to check dependencies before starting
- Clear blocking indicators when dependencies incomplete
- Source document paths for dependency verification

### Status Update Obligations
All agents must:
- Update task status as work progresses
- Verify and update dependency statuses before starting
- Mark role status in Role Assignment section
- Document blockers and dependency changes

### Agent Workflow
1. Review Role Assignment section
2. Claim available role (mark as "in_progress")
3. Check all task dependencies in source documents
4. Update dependency statuses in tasking document
5. Proceed only if dependencies complete
6. Update status regularly throughout work

### Tasking Template
Use `AGENT_TASKS/TASKING_TEMPLATE.md` when creating new task assignments. It includes all required sections for role assignment and dependency tracking.
